  "articleBody": "Nobody wants a leaky bathroom fixture, right? Those hidden drips can lead to serious water damage over time, affecting your walls, floors, and even the structural integrity of your home. The key to preventing these issues really starts with the installation process. First, it’s all about a thorough pre-installation assessment. We check your existing plumbing, water pressure, and drainage to make sure your new fixtures are compatible. It’s also crucial to coordinate with the waterproofing and tiling work, ensuring things like valve heights and drain positions are perfectly planned out. When we do the rough-in plumbing, we install supply lines, mixer valves, and drains to precise manufacturer specifications, and always pressure test everything before closing up any walls. When it comes to mounting the fixtures, whether it's a toilet, basin, or tub, we use the right fasteners, gaskets, and sealants, making sure tubs and shower bases are well-supported to prevent movement that could crack seals. The finishing touch is applying quality caulk and sealant at all joints and testing everything under normal use to catch any leaks. Remember, sealants do degrade over time, so regular checks and re-caulking are part of keeping things watertight. If you’re not confident in tackling this yourself, bringing in a pro can prevent those small drips from becoming big headaches.",
